# Line endings are a topology assumption, and this repo got it wrong once.
#
# MEASURED after the first commit: the stored blobs are pure LF (git normalised
# correctly on the way in), but `core.autocrlf=true` is set globally in
# C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig, so a fresh clone on Windows CHECKS OUT
# CRLF. biome.json pins `lineEnding: "lf"`. Result: `bun run lint:check` gave
# 25 errors on a clean clone, which means the pre-commit gate was green for the
# author and RED for anyone else who cloned it.
#
# That is the _system/CHANGE_GATE "topology" field: state what the code assumes
# about its environment, and check that the thing creating that environment
# agrees. The working tree agreed. A clone did not.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND forces LF on
# checkout on every platform, so the gate behaves identically everywhere
# regardless of anyone's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The pre-commit hook is executed by sh. CRLF in a shell script is a syntax
# error on some shells, so this one is not negotiable.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never transform these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
